body:
After the repair bank of a dead slot wins, each later slot gets ForksDetected while its parent is not rooted (forks.rs:598-602).
On Tower this does not stop, so every canonical slot gets a fork report and a WARN line.

Repro on v0.12.0 (same on v0.11.0), all 68 slots from 43 to 110 get ForksDetected:
```rust
let mut sm = BlocksStateMachine::default();
seal_at(&mut sm, 41, 40, 410, CommitmentLevel::Confirmed);
buffer(&mut sm, 42, Some(41), 10, 2);
sm.process_replay_event(dead(42).into()).unwrap();
seal_at(&mut sm, 42, 41, 11, CommitmentLevel::Confirmed);
drain(&mut sm);
let mut forked = Vec::new();
for slot in 43u64..=110 {
    seal_at(&mut sm, slot, slot - 1, slot * 10, CommitmentLevel::Confirmed);
    if slot >= 74 {
        let f = slot - 32;
        let bank = if f == 42 { 11 } else { f * 10 };
        sm.process_consensus_event(commitment(f, Some(f - 1), CommitmentLevel::Finalized, bank).into());
    }
    forked.extend(sorted_fork_reports(&drain(&mut sm)).into_iter().map(|(s, _)| s));
}
assert_eq!(forked, (43..=110).collect::<Vec<_>>());
```

Expected: no fork report for slots on the chain of the winning repair bank.
